case
@c liboctinterp/parse-tree/oct-parse.yy
-*- texinfo -*-
@deftypefn  {} {} case @var{value}
@deftypefnx {} {} case @{@var{value1}, @dots{}@}
A case statement in a switch block.

The code associated with a @code{case} statement is executed if one of the
tests below succeeds given a @code{switch} argument @var{statement} and a
@var{value} of type:

@itemize

@item number : @code{@var{statement} == @var{value}}

@item character array or string : @code{strcmp (@var{statement}, @var{value})}

@item object : @code{eq (@var{statement}, @var{value})}@*
(programmer must write overloaded @code{eq} function which performs @samp{==}) 

@item cell array : One of the @var{values} in the cell array must match
@var{statement} using the criteria above.

@end itemize

Programming Notes: Octave cases are exclusive and do not fall-through as do
@w{C-language} cases.  A @code{switch} statement must have at least one
@code{case}.

See @code{switch} for an example.
@seealso{switch}
@end deftypefn
